{"id": "2026-10-23-news-israel-orders-west-bank-wide-closure", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Israel orders West Bank-wide closure", "summary": "Netanyahu ordered a cordon on Hebron and preparation of a full West Bank closure after a checkpoint gunfight.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/23/israel-arrests-36-palestinians-in-the-west-bank-attacks-on-farmers-ramp-up", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu ordered a cordon around Hebron on the morning of Friday 23 October and told the military to \"prepare for a full closure of the entire West Bank starting today\", after soldiers killed two Palestinian gunmen in a firefight at a checkpoint near the city. At least five Israeli soldiers were wounded, two critically, according to Israel's ambulance service; witnesses said the shooting lasted about 20 minutes. Netanyahu said the army had prevented a \"major attack\" and cancelled election engagements, while National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvir called for the Palestinian Authority to be \"dismantled\". Hamas, Islamic Jihad and the PFLP praised the attack. It comes amid a surge in settler attacks on Palestinian olive harvesters, four days before Israel's general election on Tuesday 27 October.", "why": "a territory-wide closure confines Palestinians across the West Bank to their towns, and the decision is being taken in the last days of an election campaign in which West Bank policy is a central issue.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-israel-orders-west-bank-wide-closure", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Israel", "West Bank", "Hebron", "Benjamin Netanyahu"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-magnitude-7-0-quake-kills-16-in-tibet", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Magnitude 7.0 quake kills 16 in Tibet", "summary": "A M7.0 earthquake near Nagqu, Tibet killed at least 16 people per Chinese state media.", "url": "https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/eventpage/us6000u43g", "source_domain": "earthquake.usgs.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A magnitude 7.0 earthquake struck Tibet at 22:33 local time (16:33 Swiss time) on Thursday 22 October, killing at least 16 people, Chinese state media reported. The US Geological Survey placed the epicentre about 191 km east-northeast of Nagqu at a depth of 18 km and issued an orange alert, its second-highest level for expected losses. Xinhua reported more than 300 collapsed houses and at least 11 people in critical condition; state broadcaster CCTV called it the strongest quake in the region in five years. More than 1,600 people have been deployed for rescue work, and President Xi Jinping called for \"maximum\" relief efforts.", "why": "the quake hit a remote, high-altitude area as winter sets in, and casualty figures from Tibet come only through Chinese state media, so the toll may still rise.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-magnitude-7-0-quake-kills-16-in-tibet", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["China", "Tibet", "Nagqu", "USGS"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-irgc-claims-seven-more-tankers-hit-in-hormuz", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "IRGC claims seven more tankers hit in Hormuz", "summary": "Iran's IRGC claimed hits on seven more tankers near Hormuz and threatened US bases; Washington dismissed the claim.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/23/are-global-oil-reserves-sufficient-to-withstand-renewed-us-iran-war", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["disputed"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Iran's Revolutionary Guards (IRGC) said on Thursday 22 October that they had hit seven more tankers in and around the Strait of Hormuz overnight, and warned that the conflict would spread to US bases in the region if the \"trend\" continued; Washington dismissed the claim. The IRGC said four of the vessels were targeted while trying to cross by a route Iran does not authorise, and three others hit mines and were burning. This came a day after the IRGC said two tankers had been set ablaze by mines. Brent crude rose by more than $2 to $110.85 a barrel on Wednesday, close to a five-month high. Mohsen Rezaei, of Iran's Supreme National Security Council, said Iran would not send \"a single gram\" of its enriched uranium abroad.", "why": "the strait carried about a fifth of the world's oil and gas before the war that began with US-Israeli strikes on 28 February, and emergency oil stocks are already at their lowest in decades.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-irgc-claims-seven-more-tankers-hit-in-hormuz", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "IRGC", "Strait of Hormuz", "United States"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-russian-strikes-cut-power-across-ukraine", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russian strikes cut power across Ukraine", "summary": "Russian drone strikes on energy facilities caused emergency outages in eight Ukrainian regions; eight civilians killed in a day.", "url": "https://kyivindependent.com/energy-facilities-across-ukraine-targeted-as-russian-attacks-kill-at-least-8-injure-67-over-past-day/", "source_domain": "kyivindependent.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Russian strikes on Ukraine's energy system caused emergency power cuts in at least eight regions on Friday 23 October, and attacks over the past day killed eight civilians and injured 67, Ukrainian authorities said. Ukraine's air force said Russia launched 176 long-range drones overnight, 140 of which were shot down. Grid operator Ukrenergo reported outages in the Zhytomyr, Donetsk, Khmelnytskyi, Volyn, Kharkiv, Poltava, Rivne and Mykolaiv regions, and private energy company DTEK said one of its thermal power plants had stopped generating. Most of the casualties came from an attack on a market in Lozova, in the Kharkiv region, where governor Oleh Syniehubov reported 46 injured across the region.", "why": "Russia is again concentrating on power generation going into what Ukrainian officials expect to be the hardest winter of the war.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-russian-strikes-cut-power-across-ukraine", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Russia", "Ukraine", "Ukrenergo", "DTEK"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-venezuelans-march-to-demand-elections", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Venezuelans march to demand elections", "summary": "Thousands joined the first nationwide Venezuelan opposition protest in nearly two years, demanding an election date.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/23/venezuelans-demand-elections-in-first-national-protest-in-nearly-two-years", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Thousands of Venezuelans marched in Caracas and several other cities on Thursday 22 October to demand elections, the first nationwide opposition protest in nearly two years. The protest was organised by María Corina Machado's Vente Venezuela movement and held in cities including Valencia, Maracay, San Cristóbal and Maracaibo. Interim President Delcy Rodríguez has led the country since US forces captured Nicolás Maduro in a raid in January. Both she and US President Donald Trump have said elections will take place, but no date has been set; Machado, who has been abroad for almost a year, says a vote must happen by July 2027.", "why": "it is the first sign of mass street pressure on the interim government over the timetable for a successor to Maduro.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-venezuelans-march-to-demand-elections", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Venezuela", "María Corina Machado", "Delcy Rodríguez"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-ahv-funding-vote-starts-in-dead-heat", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "AHV funding vote starts in dead heat", "summary": "The first SRG/GFS Bern poll shows the VAT rise for the 13th AHV pension at 46% Yes, 49% No, and the fireworks initiative at 69% Yes.", "url": "https://www.gfsbern.ch/de/news/1-srg-trendumfrage-zur-eidg-abstimmung-vom-29-november-2026/", "source_domain": "gfsbern.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The first SRG poll for the federal votes on Sunday 29 November, published on Friday 23 October, shows the VAT increase to fund the 13th AHV/AVS pension in a dead heat with a slight lead for No: 46% Yes, 49% No. The fireworks initiative leads clearly at 69% to 29%, and the Centre party's \"Fairness\" initiative against the marriage tax penalty stands at 55% Yes, 34% No. The amendment to the War Material Act has 49% Yes and 41% No, with a split between German-speaking Switzerland (53% Yes) and Romandie (38%). GFS Bern surveyed 14,874 voters between 5 and 18 October, with a margin of error of ±2.8 points. About half of the sample was self-selected online and then weighted, and the institute stresses that this is a snapshot, not a forecast. On the AHV funding, voters aged 18–39 oppose it 56% to 35%, while over-65s back it 55%.", "why": "the result would decide whether VAT rises by 0.4 percentage points from 2028 to pay for the 13th pension, which the AHV fund will cover without extra money in 2026 and 2027.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-ahv-funding-vote-starts-in-dead-heat", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-11-29", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["GFS Bern", "SRG", "AHV"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-swiss-embassy-spouse-has-ebola-in-nigeria", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss embassy spouse has Ebola in Nigeria", "summary": "The wife of a Swiss embassy employee in Abuja was diagnosed with Ebola on 20 October, likely infected in Uganda.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/behandlung-in-nigeria-schweizerin-mit-ebola-angesteckt", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "health"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A Swiss woman, the wife of a Swiss employee at the embassy in Abuja, was diagnosed with Ebola on Tuesday 20 October and is being treated at a private clinic in the Nigerian capital, the Federal Department of Foreign Affairs (FDFA) confirmed to SRF on Friday 23 October. She probably caught the virus on a trip to Uganda about two weeks ago; the FDFA said the couple had not travelled to DR Congo, where the current outbreak began. Her husband is in isolation without symptoms. The other 25 embassy staff are well and, in agreement with Nigeria's health ministry and the WHO, do not need to isolate. Repatriation to Switzerland is being examined, and the embassy remains open.", "why": "it is a case diagnosed in Nigeria in a traveller from Uganda, a sign of how far the outbreak can travel.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-swiss-embassy-spouse-has-ebola-in-nigeria", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-20", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FDFA", "Nigeria", "Uganda", "Ebola"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-federal-council-accepts-f-35-audit-findings", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Federal Council accepts F-35 audit findings", "summary": "The Federal Council accepted six of seven CdG-N recommendations on the F-35A fixed-price affair and the seventh in part.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/IXuaTbYOxVJu", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Federal Council accepted six of the seven recommendations of the National Council's control committee (CdG-N/GPK-N) on the F-35A \"fixed price\" affair, and the seventh in part, it said on Friday 23 October. The government called the committee's 8 September report \"balanced and nuanced\". Three of the recommendations concern the duty to archive important business documents, whatever system or channel is used. The Federal Council says these are mostly already implemented and that the existing law is enough if applied consistently. Another makes armasuisse's legal service a centre of expertise. The defence department (DDPS) says it will also work more closely with parliament on large, complex procurements.", "why": "the government is accepting the criticism of how the jet purchase was documented, but it is not proposing new law.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-federal-council-accepts-f-35-audit-findings", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Council", "F-35A", "DDPS", "armasuisse"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-referendum-on-lower-cct-minimum-wages-qualifies", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Referendum on lower CCT minimum wages qualifies", "summary": "A referendum against letting extended collective agreements undercut cantonal minimum wages qualified with 66,006 valid signatures.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/-t2rtlvDYznI", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A referendum against the June amendment that lets nationally extended collective labour agreements (CCT/GAV) set minimum wages below cantonal minimum wages has qualified, the Federal Chancellery said on Friday 23 October. Of the 66,574 signatures filed on 7 October, 66,006 were valid; 50,000 are needed. A separate cantonal referendum, backed by Neuchâtel and Ticino, failed because at least eight cantons are required.", "why": "voters, not parliament, will now decide whether minimum wages set by cantons such as Neuchâtel, Geneva or Ticino can be undercut by a nationally extended sector agreement.", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-referendum-on-lower-cct-minimum-wages-qualifies", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Chancellery", "Neuchâtel", "Ticino"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-two-valais-svp-men-seek-parmelin-seat", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Two Valais SVP men seek Parmelin seat", "summary": "Michael Graber and Franz Ruppen both announced bids to succeed Guy Parmelin; Nicolas Kolly ruled himself out.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/bundesrats-kandidatur-walliser-doppelkandidatur-aeschi-ueberlegt-matter-will-nicht", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Two Upper Valais politicians, National Councillor Michael Graber and Valais government member Franz Ruppen, said at a joint press conference in Bern on Friday 23 October that they are both seeking to succeed Guy Parmelin in the Federal Council. Thomas Aeschi, leader of the SVP group in parliament, has been nominated by the Zug cantonal party but has not yet said whether he will run. Fribourg's Nicolas Kolly has ruled himself out and is aiming for the Council of States instead. Graber is known for a hard SVP line, and SRF notes that he would need votes from the left to be elected if the party puts him on its ticket. Parliament elects Parmelin's successor on Wednesday 9 December.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-two-valais-svp-men-seek-parmelin-seat", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-12-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["SVP", "Michael Graber", "Franz Ruppen", "Guy Parmelin"]}
{"id": "2026-10-23-news-sunrise-cuts-358-jobs", "date": "2026-10-23", "stream": "news", "headline": "Sunrise cuts 358 jobs", "summary": "Sunrise will cut 358 jobs after consultation, down from up to 450.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/wirtschaft/telekommunikation-sunrise-streicht-nach-konsultationsverfahren-358-jobs", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Sunrise is cutting 358 jobs after a consultation process, Switzerland's second-largest telecoms group said on Friday 23 October, down from up to 450 it had originally considered. Proposals from staff representatives and the union Syndicom lowered the number, and the social plan was improved for older employees. Together with 147 cuts announced earlier in the year, Sunrise is cutting more than 500 jobs in 2026, out of about 2,850 full-time positions.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-10-23-news-sunrise-cuts-358-jobs", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-23", "event_date": "2026-10-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Sunrise", "Syndicom"]}
